@startuml sequence-hot-standby-failover
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #01579B
    ActorBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E1F5FE
    ParticipantBorderColor #01579B
}

participant "Primary" as primary
participant "Backup" as backup
participant "Output" as output

autonumber

note over primary, backup
  Hot Standby Failover Sequence
  Primary failure detection & recovery
end note

primary ->> backup: heartbeat()
note right of primary: Periodic heartbeat (100ms)

backup ->> backup: receive_heartbeat()

primary ->> primary: process()
note right of primary: Normal operation

primary ->> backup: heartbeat()

backup ->> backup: receive_heartbeat()

primary ->> primary: CRASH!
note right of primary: Primary fails (hardware or software)

backup ->> backup: timeout_countdown()
note right of backup: Heartbeat counter starts

loop Wait for next heartbeat (500ms timeout)
    backup ->> backup: no_heartbeat_received()
end

backup ->> backup: heartbeat_timeout()
note right of backup: Timeout exceeded!\nPrimary is faulty

backup ->> backup: initiate_failover()
note right of backup: Backup activates

par Failover Sequence
    backup ->> backup: stop_replicating()
    backup ->> backup: start_processing()
    note right of backup: Backup becomes Primary
end

backup ->> output: send_output()
note right of output: New Primary sends output

output ->> output: execute()
note right of output: Output from new Primary

note over backup, output
  Failover Complete:
  1. Primary heartbeat missing for 500ms
  2. Backup detects timeout
  3. Backup stops replicating state
  4. Backup starts processing
  5. Backup becomes new Primary

  Recovery Time: < 1 second
  No output gap: Backup had state
end note

primary ->> backup: restart_attempt()
note right of primary: Primary recovers/restarts

backup ->> primary: demote_to_backup()
note right of primary: Old Primary rejoins as Backup

par New Cluster Formation
    backup ->> primary: send_state()
    note right of backup: Send current state to rejoining Primary
    primary ->> backup: ack_state()
    note right of primary: Old Primary accepts new state
end

note over backup, primary
  System Recovered:
  - New Primary: former Backup (now active)
  - New Backup: former Primary (now standby)
  - State: Consistent (transferred)
  - Operation: Resumed normally
end note

@enduml
